  "title": "Simple Quiche Lorraine",
  "description": "Make this easy quiche Lorraine featuring eggs, bacon, onion, and Swiss cheese baked in a store-bought crust, and serve it for any meal of the day!",
  "authors": [
    "Lynn"
  ],
  "date_published": "2000-04-11T21:40:44-04:00",
  "date_modified": "2025-10-28T12:14:53-04:00",
  "prep_time": "PT20M",
  "cook_time": "PT50M",
  "total_time": "PT80M",
  "yield": [
    "8",
    "1 (9-inch) quiche"
  ],
  "categories": [
    "Brunch"
  ],
  "cuisines": [
    "French"
  ],
  "regions": [
    "French"
  ],
  "breadcrumbs": [],
  "keywords": [],
  "ingredients": [
    "1 (9 inch) refrigerated pie pastry",
    "6 slices bacon",
    "1 medium onion, sliced",
    "1.5 cups shredded Swiss cheese",
    "1 tablespoon all-purpose flour",
    "1.5 cups milk",
    "3 large eggs, beaten",
    "0.25 teaspoon salt"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Preheat the oven to 450 degrees F (230 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/y17WY568CvO9MyRq6XuJ5RVNmqU=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-01-81056132cda64472af7d179a6a86995c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place pie pastry into a 9-inch pie pan; line with a double layer of aluminum foil and a layer of pie weights or dried beans.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/d7KzCwkItFFfgSy0E4A1NxhwIQQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-02-a9426faccfcf495f84523bc029cb381b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until golden on the edges, about 8 minutes. Carefully remove the foil and weights; continue baking until crust is set and dry, about 5 minutes more. Remove from the oven and reduce the temperature to 325 degrees F (165 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/IkIdgjvRqskBqdfSO1-jb9HvXpQ=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-03-a4f8458e4308431c826fce46266b6479.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the crust is baking, cook bacon in a large skillet over medium-high heat until crisp, about 10 minutes. Transfer to a paper towel-lined plate and crumble when cool enough to handle. Drain all but 2 tablespoons drippings from the skillet.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/2yJM3RNV4F7QBlYZg7q53IWf7M0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-04-3130e100673a46ca96500d11cc617d09.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add onion to drippings in the skillet; cook and stir over medium heat until tender, about 5 minutes. Use a slotted spoon and transfer to a bowl.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/8m7My0xsz4VqI_5AOo2z8PfDFHs=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-05-aa452aec1dd5414ebbd544e9bb5ebf8e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Toss Swiss cheese and flour together in a small bowl. Whisk milk, eggs, and salt together in a large bowl, then stir in bacon and onion.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/A9TVFGwrElV738c2jZfXHFJKeM0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-06-321dd100a4f54648bf5da244348f1b75.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_06.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix in cheese mixture until well combined, then pour into pie crust.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MnWaS9J7KdXjyNSoNldW7h58wK0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-07-ebb658c556c04ffca8fc47afa778bfd4.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_07.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the preheated oven until a knife inserted into the center comes out clean, 35 to 40 minutes. Let stand for 10 minutes before serving.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/bLgbT8vHfWN3-aaKC-BdgBOaZRc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/ALR-18477-quiche-lorraine-ii-VAT-step-08-9a928dd94a6b4483919c970b31442c6b.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/18477/step_08.webp"
    }
  ],
